   },
   "harm": "changing -bind semantics breaks setups that listen on one IP but load balance outbound connections",
   "hash": "91d1ab611e7be3db",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4216096603",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4216096603",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "This might break a scenario where someone wants to listen on one IP, but load balance outgoing connections. A new option might be better?",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-23",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "c:4524241991",
    "quote": "Added `-outboundbind=<addr>` as a separate option instead of extending `-bind`"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#issuecomment-4216096603"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-04-14",
   "author": "frankomosh",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3793780005"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5baa78a79cb0c2144b680360d3bb46d223546df3"
   },
   "harm": "storing the address without early validation silently kills outbound connections rather than failing loudly at startup",
   "hash": "45935cee4dd18a5b",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3078339596",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3078339596",
   "kind": "safety",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "misconfigured address fails loudly at init rather than silently killing outbound for that family",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-08-17",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "rc:3793780005",
    "quote": "Done. `IsAddrBindable()` does a trial `bind()` at init, so a misconfigured address fails startup."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#discussion_r3078339596"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-04-25",
   "author": "gmaxwell",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4319952452",
    "c:4524241991"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5baa78a79cb0c2144b680360d3bb46d223546df3"
   },
   "harm": "binding outbound connections via -bind prevents the node from connecting to peers on the local LAN or VM bridge interfaces",
   "hash": "1a48bb8a3328fc9b",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4317621161",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4317621161",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "as proposed here -bind=mypublicinterface would suddenly make my node unable to connect to stuff on my local lan (or, in VM on bridge interfaces)-- pretty surprising.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-23",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "c:4524241991",
    "quote": "Kept `-bind` semantics unchanged, so existing setups (including LAN/bridge peers) are unaffected"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#issuecomment-4317621161"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-09",
   "author": "vasild",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3793780883",
    "rc:3793781233"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5baa78a79cb0c2144b680360d3bb46d223546df3"
   },
   "harm": "allowing port numbers in -outboundbind causes confusion since outgoing source ports should not be specified",
   "hash": "b061ed5dbba64eef",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3380992855",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3380992855",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "this will allow ports to be included, e.g. `-outboundbind=1.2.4.5:5678` which better not be allowed to avoid confusion.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-08-17",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "rc:3793781233",
    "quote": "switched to `LookupHost()` so a port is rejected at startup."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#discussion_r3380992855"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-09",
   "author": "vasild",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3793782102"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5baa78a79cb0c2144b680360d3bb46d223546df3"
   },
   "harm": "silently swallowing unusable addresses masks configuration errors",
   "hash": "77177a6c42918c53",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3381134818",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3381134818",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "What's the reason to silently swallow such addresses? It would be more obvious if we return an error for those at startup, like we do for invalid values.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-08-17",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "rc:3793782102",
    "quote": "Nothing is dropped silently."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#discussion_r3381134818"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-10",
   "author": "vasild",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3793783043"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "first-wins prevents overriding earlier configuration settings",
   "hash": "221ea03f863c4f4c",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:28:09+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3387250516",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3387250516",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Usually the notion is that the last one wins. E.g. `-outboundbind=1.2.3.4 -outboundbind=5.6.7.8` -- `5.6.7.8` should be used. This helps override earlier settings which might be out of one's control.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-08-17",
    "by": "8144225309",
    "id": "rc:3793783043",
    "quote": "first-wins matches the config-file convention (\"the first one is generally chosen\", doc/bitcoin-conf.md; reverse_precedence in common/settings.cpp)."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35027#discussion_r3387250516"
  }
 ],
